# DNS and Tailnet

This design keeps internal naming and remote access tight. It does not pretend the tailnet is another trusted VLAN.

## DNS Model

- Internal suffix: `{{ dns.zone }}`
- Primary internal resolver: AdGuard Home on `{{ dns.primary_resolver.host }}` (`{{ dns.primary_resolver.address }}`)
- DNS authority: local records and aliases in AdGuard Home
- Recursive DNS: AdGuard for `management`, `server`, `lan`, `iot`, and `tv`; public recursion for `guest` and `work`
- Public app domain: `{{ dns.public_domain.zone }}`, served from the `edge` zone rather than AdGuard Home
- Private tailnet app domain: `{{ dns.private_tailnet_domain.zone }}`
- Tailnet-native private names: MagicDNS on the tailnet `{{ tailnet.private_naming.tailnet_native_namespace }}` namespace

## Naming Shape

The namespace is flat:

- Device names: `mgmt-router-01.{{ dns.zone }}`, `server-ha-01.{{ dns.zone }}`
- Service aliases: `dns.{{ dns.zone }}`, `adguard.{{ dns.zone }}`, `ha.{{ dns.zone }}`, `nas.{{ dns.zone }}`, `proxy.{{ dns.zone }}`

Do not invent per-zone subdomains. The flat namespace is simpler.

There are four naming layers in this design:

- `{{ dns.zone }}` for homelab services reached over split DNS
- `{{ dns.private_tailnet_domain.zone }}` for private tailnet-only app and server names on your own domain
- Tailnet MagicDNS names for devices that join the tailnet directly, especially edge servers
- `{{ dns.public_domain.zone }}` for public HTTP(S) entrypoints on the edge

Do not collapse those into one namespace. They solve different problems.

## AdGuard Home Role

AdGuard Home does four jobs:

- recursive DNS for approved local VLANs
- local records for `{{ dns.zone }}`
- DNS filtering
- split DNS target for the tailnet

Guest does not receive internal records. Work does not receive internal records.

`{{ dns.public_domain.zone }}` is separate. Public DNS for `*.{{ dns.public_domain.zone }}` lives outside AdGuard Home and points at the edge proxy. Do not try to make AdGuard Home authoritative for the public domain.

The private `{{ dns.private_tailnet_domain.zone }}` zone is different. It resolves only for tailnet users, using Tailscale split DNS to reach AdGuard Home.

